---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import RegisterStructureDemo from "../../components/RegisterStructureDemo.astro";
import StructureFacts from "../../components/StructureFacts.astro";
import TermCallout from "../../components/TermCallout.astro";
import "../../styles/set-lesson.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="MvRegister"
  description="Alice and Bob keep concurrent trail-status reports until Carol can inspect and resolve them."
  territory="Structures"
  sheetTitle="MvRegister"
>
  <article class="register-lesson">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="territory-label">Structures</p>
      <h1>MvRegister</h1>
      <p class="structure-summary">
        The ranger cannot discard Alice's open report or Bob's closed report.
        Carol must see both before she walks to Eagle Creek and resolves the
        disagreement.
      </p>
    </header>

    <StructureFacts
      family="CRDT"
      model="State-based multi-value register"
      updates="Causally tagged string writes"
      merge="Keep writes that are concurrent; replace only observed history."
      delivery="Safe under repeated and out-of-order delivery"
      bestFor="One field where valid concurrent answers need explicit resolution"
      cost="Surviving values, write identities, and causal context"
    />

    <section aria-labelledby="siblings-title">
      <h2 id="siblings-title">The disagreement remains visible</h2>
      <p>
        A <dfn><a href="/glossary/#multi-value-register">multi-value register</a></dfn>
        {" "}keeps concurrent writes as alternatives, often called siblings.
        Alice had not seen Bob's report, and Bob had not seen Alice's, so
        neither write replaces the other.
      </p>
      <TermCallout
        term="multi-value register"
        definition="A replicated register that retains concurrent writes until a write that observes them supersedes them."
      />
      <figure>
        <table aria-label="Concurrent MvRegister reports">
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">Replica</th><th scope="col">Visible alternatives after merge</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row">Alice</th><td>Trail closed · Trail open</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Bob</th><td>Trail closed · Trail open</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Carol</th><td>Trail closed · Trail open</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <figcaption>Convergence can preserve a conflict instead of hiding it.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <RegisterStructureDemo
      kind="mv-register"
      title="Keep both trail reports"
      description="Alice and Bob write without observing each other. Exchange both deltas and inspect the alternatives that every notebook retains."
      rule="Keep concurrent writes as siblings."
      raceLabel="Race Alice's and Bob's reports"
    />

    <section aria-labelledby="resolve-title">
      <h2 id="resolve-title">Carol resolves what she observed</h2>
      <p>
        Carol inspects the bridge, reads both alternatives, and writes a new
        status. That write replaces the siblings in her causal history. It
        cannot erase an unseen report from an offline hiker.
      </p>
      <p>
        The deeper Atlas lab exposes the write tags, causal context, delayed
        messages, and observed resolution step.
      </p>
      <p class="lesson-entry">
        <a href="/atlas/multi-value-registers/">Open the causal MvRegister lab</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="source-title">
      <h2 id="source-title">Sources and implementation</h2>
      <p>
        The demo runs Watershed's{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/tylerbutler/watershed/blob/4a8739323ee491f353fcaa8ccfb0488419c1cd43/src/watershed/mv_register_kernel.gleam">MV-register kernel</a>
        {" "}through the Atlas toolkit.
      </p>
    </section>

    <nav class="structure-next" aria-label="Continue through register structures">
      <a href="/structures/lww-register/">Back to LWWRegister</a>
      <a href="/structures/registers/">Browse register family</a>
      <a href="/structures/register-collection/">Continue to RegisterCollection</a>
    </nav>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .lesson-entry {
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
</style>
